  "slug": "decoding-mitochondrial-diverse-eukaryotes-557a",
  "summary": "Long-read and short-read RNA-seq now feed transcript-level tools benchmarked against established quantifiers and internal controls.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is transcript-level resolution of RNA-seq data. IG-28 identifies high-confidence isoforms from large bulk and single-cell full-length cDNA sets and reports outperforming other tools in benchmarks. GaussF performs alignment-free isoform quantification using GC-stratified k-mer Gaussian CDF self-benchmarking and is evaluated against Kallisto and Salmon. A minimal-sharing k-mer strategy isolates transcript-specific regions to reduce mapping ambiguity, while CALMeR conditions long-read MAPQ filtering on transcript context, improving spike-in transcript recovery over fixed thresholds. Several items extend this resolution beyond quantification: tWhEEL links transcript assembly to CRISPR knockout feasibility, SQANTI-evidence annotates unannotated genomes from long-read RNA-seq, and LRP2 integrates isoform discovery with mass-spectrometry evidence at the protein level. Edi-Set-Flow and the mitochondrial RNA processing tool address narrower RNA-level questions. A recurring feature is internal validation, as GaussF pairs a built-in self-benchmark with comparison against Kallisto and Salmon.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-04"
}
